# Problem: Java me Pass by Value hota hai
Java pass by value language hai.
Matlab jab swap(a, b) call karte hai, to:
• a ki copy method me jaati hai
• b ki copy method me jaati hai
• Original a aur b change nahi hote

Isliye output same rehta hai.

🔎 Step by Step Samjho
swap(a,b);

To, Ye actually internally aise kaam karta hai: swap(10,20);

Method ke andar:
public static void swap(int a, int b){
    int temp = a;  // temp = 10
    a = b;         // a = 20
    b = temp;      // b = 10
}

👉 Ye sirf method ke local variables change hue
👉 Main method ke a aur b same rehte hain

✅ Output kya aayega?
Input:
10
20

Output:
10 20
10 20

✅ Solution 1 (Return Method Use Karo)
=> Swap karne ke liye return use karo:

public static int[] swap(int a, int b){
    int temp = a;
    a = b;
    b = temp;
    return new int[]{a,b};
}

In, Main method:
int result[] = swap(a,b);
a = result[0];
b = result[1];

✅ Solution 2 (Using Array – Best for Learning)
public static void swap(int arr[]){
    int temp = arr[0];
    arr[0] = arr[1];
    arr[1] = temp;
}

Main:
int arr[] = {a,b};
swap(arr);
System.out.println(arr[0] + " " + arr[1]);

🧠 Interview Important Point
👉 Java me primitive types (int, float, char) always pass by value
👉 Java me pass by reference hota hi nahi hai.

================================== Topics: Array, Que: PrintNegativeElements =============================
🔹 2nd Method (Input + Print together)
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    arr[i] = sc.nextInt();
    if (arr[i] < 0){
        System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
    }
}
✔ Advantage:
Thoda short code
Memory same use ho rahi hai

❌ Problem:
Single Responsibility Principle break karta hai
Ek hi loop me:
    input bhi le raha
    logic bhi laga raha
    print bhi kar raha

Agar baad me tumhe:
    positive count nikalna ho
    sum nikalna ho
    array reuse karna ho

To problem ho sakti hai.

🔹 1st Method (Input and Processing separate) ✅
for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++) {
    arr[i] = sc.nextInt();
}

for (int i = 0; i < arr.length; i++){
    if (arr[i] < 0)
        System.out.print(arr[i] + " ");
}
✔ Advantage:
Clean structure
Readable
Debug karna easy
Industry standard approach
Reusable array

Ye professional coding style hai 💯

🎯 Final Verdict
👉 Interview / Best Practice → 2nd Method
👉 Quick coding / simple question → 1st Method bhi chalega

💡 Pro Developer Tip: Agar sirf negative print karna hai aur array store karna zaroori nahi hai, tab 1st method efficient hai.
Lekin agar DSA practice kar rahe ho to: 🔥 Always separate Input, Processing, and Output.

